    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d814">

                <pb facs="0754" n="742" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg742"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00111 A.R./1096: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panama</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-18T16:00:00-05:00">May 18, 1940—4
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 5 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>70. My telegram No. 69. At the suggestion of Uruguayan Foreign Minister Dr. Garay
                    has just furnished the press the following additional communiqué: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“In connection with the joint declaration of the American Republics the
                            Panamanian Foreign Office states that the Government of Colombia, in
                            adhering to the said document, expressed the desire that the names of
                            Denmark and Norway be added to those of the three countries whose
                            neutrality has been violated by the German forces.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
